WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.754 --> 00:00:13.155
more Jo got to know Laurie the more she liked him.

2
00:00:14.456 --> 00:00:20.400
She found that her preconceptions about his privileged upbringing and the behavior she expected from someone so wealthy

3
00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:21.460
were quickly shattered.

4
00:00:22.841 --> 00:00:27.024
For Jo had never met anyone as down-to-earth, sincere, and witty as Laurie.

5
00:00:28.436 --> 00:00:32.078
However, what happened later on that evening really clinched their friendship.

6
00:00:34.079 --> 00:00:39.881
The two young people were exchanging jokes and laughing rather loudly when Meg, who had been dancing almost

7
00:00:39.941 --> 00:00:42.762
the entire evening, limped over to where they sat.

8
00:00:42.782 --> 00:00:47.925
"Jo," Meg whispered, her face pinched with pain.

9
00:00:49.065 --> 00:00:50.546
"Meg! What's the matter?"

10
00:00:50.966 --> 00:00:52.447
Jo exclaimed, alarmed.

11
00:00:52.467 --> 00:00:58.502
"I've hurt my ankle," answered Meg, tenderly massaging the swollen area.

12
00:00:58.522 --> 00:01:01.923
"Oh, dear, what are we going to do?"

13
00:01:02.484 --> 00:01:03.724
Jo cracked her knuckles.

14
00:01:03.744 --> 00:01:06.266
"Jo! Don't do that!

15
00:01:06.546 --> 00:01:07.807
That's so ill-mannered!"

16
00:01:08.487 --> 00:01:11.909
Meg, in her agony, still worried about how others might perceive them.

17
00:01:11.929 --> 00:01:14.570
"Can I help in any way?"

18
00:01:14.911 --> 00:01:16.251
Laurie gallantly interrupted.

19
00:01:16.271 --> 00:01:19.913
"No, silly boy," Jo brushed him aside.

20
00:01:19.933 --> 00:01:24.456
"It took us twenty minutes to walk here," she calculated to Meg.

21
00:01:25.612 --> 00:01:29.033
"If I carry you, we may be able to get home in less than an hour."

22
00:01:29.053 --> 00:01:33.214
"No!" Meg and Laurie cried out simultaneously.

23
00:01:33.234 --> 00:01:40.376
"We can't afford to hire a carriage, Meg," said Jo decisively, "so unless you want to ask Sallie

24
00:01:40.416 --> 00:01:44.518
whether or not they can accommodate you for the night, then I don't see any other way."

25
00:01:45.578 --> 00:01:50.819
Indeed, Jo spoke truthfully, since the Marches no longer had a carriage and the girls certainly did not

26
00:01:50.859 --> 00:01:53.000
have enough money to hire one to take them back.

27
00:01:55.016 --> 00:02:02.442
"Well, I was planning to return home soon," said Laurie, clearing his throat then continuing, "and I have

28
00:02:02.482 --> 00:02:02.983
a carriage.

29
00:02:03.784 --> 00:02:08.567
If you would do me the honor of escorting you back home, then I shall be the envy

30
00:02:08.608 --> 00:02:10.149
of all the lads here tonight."

31
00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:13.572
Jo appreciated Laurie's tact and kindness.

32
00:02:14.532 --> 00:02:19.036
The two sisters heartily accepted Laurie's offer and they rode home in luxury and comfort.

33
00:02:20.257 --> 00:02:23.240
The following day was their last day of freedom, as Jo put it.

34
00:02:25.036 --> 00:02:29.799
The winter holidays were coming to a close and the girls would be returning to their normal activities.

35
00:02:30.819 --> 00:02:33.121
For Meg and Jo, that meant going back to work.

36
00:02:34.121 --> 00:02:37.063
Meg worked as a governess for the King family and their children.

37
00:02:37.863 --> 00:02:42.646
Although she took great pleasure in making her own living, Meg sometimes found it a challenge to be

38
00:02:42.706 --> 00:02:45.968
surrounded by wealth and luxuries that she knew she would never possess.

39
00:02:45.988 --> 00:02:55.761
"It frustrates me how wealthy some families are, while others are so deprived," she often complained upon returning

40
00:02:55.801 --> 00:02:57.041
from her place of employment.

41
00:02:58.121 --> 00:03:02.043
As for Jo, she worked as a companion to their rich old Aunt March.

42
00:03:03.503 --> 00:03:08.185
Every morning when Jo arrived at the mansion, Aunt March presented her with a list of things to

43
00:03:08.225 --> 00:03:08.925
do that day.

44
00:03:10.725 --> 00:03:16.867
Often the list included petty things like brushing Polly, the pet parrot, and feeding her crackers, or changing

45
00:03:16.907 --> 00:03:18.548
the order of the cushions on the sofa.

46
00:03:19.516 --> 00:03:23.737
Of course, one thing Aunt March always wrote down was for Jo to read to her from a

47
00:03:23.797 --> 00:03:25.618
book of the old lady's choice.

48
00:03:26.658 --> 00:03:31.019
Needless to say, Jo's favorite part of the day was when she could escape into the pages of

49
00:03:31.059 --> 00:03:32.120
an imaginary world.

50
00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:38.302
"At least you girls get reimbursed for your diligent efforts," whined Amy.

51
00:03:39.342 --> 00:03:44.123
Though it was a holiday period, Mother made sure the girls had plenty to do around the house

52
00:03:44.603 --> 00:03:46.044
so they did not become lazy.

53
00:03:47.048 --> 00:03:51.109
Meg was shortening the hem of some of her old dresses so Amy could wear them to school.

54
00:03:52.009 --> 00:03:54.010
Jo was sitting and darning some old socks.

55
00:03:55.050 --> 00:03:58.231
What little silverware the Marches had, Amy was polishing.

56
00:03:59.311 --> 00:04:04.933
And Beth, who at the age of thirteen still loved her dolls, was mending some button eyes on

57
00:04:05.053 --> 00:04:05.993
one of her "children."

58
00:04:06.013 --> 00:04:08.394
"What do you mean, Amy?"

59
00:04:08.994 --> 00:04:12.315
Meg asked lightly as she adjusted the cushion under her injured ankle.

60
00:04:13.395 --> 00:04:18.929
"I am forced to learn things I have no interest in," Amy began, her cheeks flushed pink.

61
00:04:18.949 --> 00:04:23.272
"Girls tease me all the time about my dresses or ribbons.

62
00:04:24.172 --> 00:04:28.455
And I don't get paid for any of the abuse I suffer daily like you do."

63
00:04:29.656 --> 00:04:33.478
Jo rolled her eyes and said, "No one gets paid to go to school.

64
00:04:34.398 --> 00:04:39.982
And besides," she added, using her needle to point to Meg and herself, "we had to go to

65
00:04:40.022 --> 00:04:41.582
school just the same as you."

66
00:04:42.583 --> 00:04:43.904
Meg put her sewing down.

67
00:04:44.476 --> 00:04:46.657
"If only our lives were different, girls."

68
00:04:47.918 --> 00:04:49.398
"What would you change, Meg?"

69
00:04:49.798 --> 00:04:50.319
asked Beth.

70
00:04:51.059 --> 00:04:56.021
She had finished "surgery" on one doll and was moving on to replace a torn-off limb on another

71
00:04:56.121 --> 00:04:56.821
worn-out one.

72
00:04:56.841 --> 00:05:01.623
"Well, I wouldn't work for the Kings," Meg said after a while.

73
00:05:01.643 --> 00:05:08.606
"I would find an agreeable job, perhaps as a seamstress so that I might design beautiful gowns for

74
00:05:08.686 --> 00:05:09.606
ladies to wear."

75
00:05:09.626 --> 00:05:14.509
"But you wouldn't be able to wear them yourself," said Jo candidly.

76
00:05:15.530 --> 00:05:20.453
Meg gave her a hurt look and continued, "There might be some material left for me to make

77
00:05:20.513 --> 00:05:21.274
my own dress."

78
00:05:21.294 --> 00:05:28.599
"Then you would look like Beth's doll there," Jo laughed, pointing to one doll who wore an ugly

79
00:05:28.639 --> 00:05:31.401
dress made out of different scraps of fabric sewn together.

80
00:05:31.421 --> 00:05:33.502
"That's mean, Jo.

81
00:05:33.922 --> 00:05:38.485
I just want a better life for myself and my family," was Meg's tearful reply.

82
00:05:38.505 --> 00:05:41.848
"Sorry, Meg," apologized Jo.

83
00:05:43.024 --> 00:05:46.505
"As for me, I'd be happy if Aunt March took longer naps."

84
00:05:47.525 --> 00:05:52.807
The sisters shared a hearty giggle over this as they knew how cranky and bossy their old relative

85
00:05:52.847 --> 00:05:58.188
was. Jo often blamed Aunt March's bad moods on her lack of sleep.

86
00:05:59.269 --> 00:06:01.169
"What would you do while she's sleeping?"

87
00:06:01.569 --> 00:06:02.089
asked Beth.

88
00:06:02.109 --> 00:06:08.111
"Go to her library, of course, and read every single book," was Jo's matter-of-fact reply.

89
00:06:08.131 --> 00:06:17.051
"Well," Beth said in her soft and mild manner, "if only I wasn't so shy I would love

90
00:06:17.091 --> 00:06:19.313
to earn some money and buy a piano."

91
00:06:20.453 --> 00:06:25.576
Her sisters gave her an encouraging nod for they knew how Beth's shyness hindered her from the everyday

92
00:06:25.616 --> 00:06:28.498
activities others took for granted, like going to school.

93
00:06:28.518 --> 00:06:33.561
"If only I didn't have to go to school," whined Amy.

94
00:06:33.581 --> 00:06:38.084
"I wouldn't have to hear those degrading remarks about my attire."

95
00:06:39.228 --> 00:06:44.670
Though she moaned about school all the time, Amy never missed an opportunity to use new words she

96
00:06:44.710 --> 00:06:48.711
had learned there or to tell her sisters something interesting she had just been taught.

97
00:06:48.731 --> 00:06:54.873
"Your dresses are lovely," chirped Meg, since they used to belong to her at one time.

98
00:06:54.893 --> 00:07:03.275
"But they're so outdated," retorted Amy, adding, "although some girls do say rather pleasant things about my hair."

99
00:07:03.935 --> 00:07:05.516
She fluffed and patted her curls.

100
00:07:06.804 --> 00:07:10.887
Her sisters silently chuckled at Amy's open vanity about her beauty trademark.

101
00:07:10.907 --> 00:07:18.371
"And if only I had a straight elegant nose," Amy complained, pinching the ridge of her nose and

102
00:07:18.471 --> 00:07:20.993
tugging at it as if that would restructure it.

103
00:07:21.013 --> 00:07:28.057
"As much as we would all like our 'if only' stories to come true," broke in Meg, "the

104
00:07:28.097 --> 00:07:32.800
reality is that tomorrow life will return to just as it was a few weeks ago."

105
00:07:33.824 --> 00:07:36.928
"And there is not much we can do about it," concluded Jo.

106
00:07:38.130 --> 00:07:42.516
The sisters harmoniously let out a wistful collective sigh and resumed their work.
